---
title: Tuscany Chicken
description: Seared chicken breasts simmered in a creamy parmesan sauce with sun-dried tomatoes and spinach.
course: Main
cuisine: Italian
servings: 4
time required: 35 minutes
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
source: https://downshiftology.com/recipes/creamy-tuscan-chicken/
image: https://i2.wp.com/www.downshiftology.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/Tuscan-Chicken-main-1.jpg
tags: [chicken, creamy, italian, skillet, low-carb]
---

Season both sides of @boneless skinless chicken breasts{4}(6-ounce each) with @Italian seasoning{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1%tsp}, and @freshly ground black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

Heat @extra virgin olive oil{2%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium heat. Sear the chicken for ~{3-4%minutes} per side until golden, then remove to a plate.

Add another @extra virgin olive oil{1%tbsp} and the @yellow onion{1/4%cup}(finely chopped) to the same skillet. Sauté for ~{2-3%minutes} until softened.

Add @sun-dried tomatoes{1/2%cup}(thinly sliced) and @garlic{4%cloves}(minced); sauté for ~{1%minute} until fragrant.

Add @baby spinach{2%cups} and sauté for ~{1%minute} until it just begins to wilt.

Add @heavy cream{1.5%cups} and @parmesan{1/4%cup}(freshly grated), stir together, and bring to a simmer.

Return the chicken to the skillet and cook until heated through, about ~{5%minutes}.
